# The sky's moods, one landscape at a time, played through the real game:
# a squall off the sea, dawn mist lying in the moss, a whiteout on the
# snowfield, dry lightning over the bonelands, ash falling on the burning at
# dusk, and a wet village night mirroring its lights.
#   tools/tour.sh tours/sky.tour --seed=1
coast calm
# The coast: bleak grey afternoon, a squall coming in off the sea.
place coast
hour 15
weather rain:1
wait 1.0
shot 01-coast-squall
walk 1,-1 1.5
shot 02-coast-squall-walked
# The moss at dawn: the mist the rules lay in its hollows, then drizzle into it.
place moss
hour 6.4
weather clear:0
wait 1.0
shot 03-moss-dawn-mist
weather drizzle:0.8
wait 1.0
shot 04-moss-drizzle-in-mist
# The snowfield: snow in squalls, then the horizon goes.
place snowfield
hour 13
weather snow:1
wait 1.0
shot 05-snowfield-snow-squall
weather whiteout:1
wait 1.0
shot 06-snowfield-whiteout
# The bonelands: hard glare at noon, then a dry storm at dusk: blown dust,
# a devil and sheet flickers before the first strike, then its afterglow.
place bonelands
hour 12.5
weather glare:1
wait 1.0
shot 07-bonelands-glare
hour 20.2
weather dry_storm:1
wait 0.5
shot 08-bonelands-dry-storm
await strike 60
wait 0.12
shot 09-bonelands-afterglow
# A few frames on: the light has rolled on through the cloud and let go.
wait 0.25
shot 09b-bonelands-afterglow-rolls
# The burning at dusk: ash fall, then the furnace haze.
place burning
hour 19.4
weather ash:1
wait 1.0
shot 10-burning-ash-dusk
weather haze:1
wait 1.0
shot 11-burning-furnace-haze
# A wet night in the first village: lamps, fires and neon in the puddles, and
# their shafts in the rain.
village 0
hour 22.5
weather rain:0.8
wait 1.0
shot 12-village-wet-night
tap lamp
wait 0.5
shot 13-village-wet-lantern with lamp
weather rules
